"segments": [
{
"start": 5.16,
"end": 7.14,
"text": " We broke off, but not for long."
},
{
"start": 7.82,
"end": 10.4,
"text": "Next up were my worries about the children."
},
{
"start": 15.74,
"end": 20.75,
"text": "When I was talking to Prince one day, he said to me that he didn't have a mother."
},
{
"start": 21.99,
"end": 22.99,
"text": "He said he didn't have a mother?"
},
{
"start": 23.05,
"end": 25.67,
"text": "Yeah, I said, Prince, where's your mummy?"
},
{
"start": 25.99,
"end": 27.35,
"text": "And he said, I haven't got a mother."
},
{
"start": 29.19,
"end": 29.61,
"text": " That's right."
},
{
"start": 30.69,
"end": 31.75,
"text": "Did you tell him to say that?"
},
{
"start": 32.29,
"end": 32.47,
"text": "No."
},
{
"start": 33.11,
"end": 34.89,
"text": "What do you think he means when he says I haven't got a mother?"
},
{
"start": 35.93,
"end": 37.31,
"text": "Like he said, he didn't have a mother."
},
{
"start": 38.71,
"end": 42.52,
"text": "Do you not think, though, that your children would benefit from contact with their mother?"
},
{
"start": 44.0,
"end": 46.28,
"text": "No, cos she doesn't..."
},
{
"start": 47.16,
"end": 48.18,
"text": "It's private information."
},
{
"start": 48.22,
"end": 53.16,
"text": "She doesn't... She can't handle it."
},
{
"start": 54.02,
"end": 55.28,
"text": "She can't handle her own children?"
},
{
"start": 55.98,
"end": 58.12,
"text": "She'd prefer them be with me than with her."
},
{
"start": 59.79,
"end": 63.77,
"text": " Did you know that she didn't want to have relationships with the children when you married her?"
},
{
"start": 64.43,
"end": 64.63,
"text": "Yeah."
},
{
"start": 65.55,
"end": 66.37,
"text": "She did it for me."
},
{
"start": 67.27,
"end": 67.97,
"text": "She did it for me."
},
{
"start": 68.72,
"end": 72.5,
"text": "So, just that I understand this correctly... She's a wonderful person, too."
},
{
"start": 72.64,
"end": 75.52,
"text": "She knew that Michael Jackson loves children."
},
{
"start": 75.86,
"end": 76.2,
"text": "Yeah."
},
{
"start": 76.34,
"end": 78.32,
"text": "And she knew that Michael Jackson wanted children."
},
{
"start": 78.36,
"end": 79.16,
"text": "That's why."
},
{
"start": 79.46,
"end": 80.96,
"text": "She said, you need to be a daddy."
},
{
"start": 82.72,
"end": 83.0,
"text": "Right."
},
{
"start": 84.48,
"end": 85.66,
"text": "She said you needed to be a daddy."
},
{
"start": 85.8,
"end": 86.8,
"text": "Mm-hm."
},
{
"start": 86.82,
"end": 88.2,
"text": "More than she needed to be a mother."
},
{
"start": 88.5,
"end": 91.36,
"text": " Yeah, and she wanted to do that for me as a present."
},
{
"start": 94.94,
"end": 95.58,
"text": "As a present?"
},
{
"start": 95.94,
"end": 97.1,
"text": "Yeah, yeah."
},
{
"start": 97.74,
"end": 98.28,
"text": "What do you mean?"
},
{
"start": 98.94,
"end": 99.61,
"text": "It's a gift."
},
{
"start": 99.84,
"end": 101.81,
"text": "I used to walk around holding baby dolls."
},
{
"start": 102.95,
"end": 103.21,
"text": "Really?"
},
{
"start": 103.57,
"end": 105.61,
"text": "Yeah, because I wanted children so badly."
},
{
"start": 105.91,
"end": 113.51,
"text": "What you've just said is that your wife gave you two children as a present because she knew you wanted to be a father."
},
{
"start": 113.69,
"end": 114.99,
"text": "Yeah, that's a lovely gesture."
},
{
"start": 115.63,
"end": 116.89,
"text": "Well, it's an incredible gesture."
},
{
"start": 117.15,
"end": 119.55,
"text": " Yeah, there are surrogate mothers who do that every day."
},
{
"start": 119.57,
"end": 121.81,
"text": "It happens every day in the world."
},
{
"start": 122.0,
"end": 123.19,
"text": "It's happening right now."
},
{
"start": 123.32,
"end": 124.92,
"text": "Is that how Blanket was born as well?"
},
{
"start": 125.26,
"end": 127.98,
"text": "I used a surrogate mother of my own sperm cells."
},
{
"start": 128.64,
"end": 131.0,
"text": "I had my own sperm cells of my other two children."
},
{
"start": 131.14,
"end": 132.14,
"text": "They're all my children."
},
{
"start": 132.42,
"end": 133.7,
"text": "But I used a surrogate mother."
},
{
"start": 134.36,
"end": 136.72,
"text": "And she doesn't know me, I don't know her."
},
{
"start": 137.48,
"end": 139.28,
"text": "And that's how I was born."
},
{
"start": 139.75,
"end": 141.89,
"text": " How did you select the mother out of interest?"
},
{
"start": 142.05,
"end": 144.01,
"text": "It didn't matter to me, as long as she was healthy."
},
{
"start": 144.03,
"end": 150.6,
"text": "I didn't care what race, I said, as long as she's healthy and she doesn't have..."
},
{
"start": 150.68,
"end": 156.22,
"text": "Her vision's good and her intellect, I want to know how intelligent she is."
},
{
"start": 157.0,
"end": 162.82,
"text": "Would you have had... Would you have conceived a child with a black woman?"
},
{
"start": 163.22,
"end": 163.66,
"text": "Of course."
},
{
"start": 163.72,
"end": 164.39,
"text": "As a surrogate mother?"
},
{
"start": 164.83,
"end": 165.39,
"text": "Of course."
},
{
"start": 167.57,
"end": 170.98,
"text": " I've seen Blanket, and I think, safe to say, his mother was probably white."
},
{
"start": 171.68,
"end": 172.42,
"text": "No, you're wrong."
},
{
"start": 172.8,
"end": 173.18,
"text": "I'm wrong?"
},
{
"start": 173.7,
"end": 173.88,
"text": "Yeah."
},
{
"start": 174.06,
"end": 174.46,
"text": "Oh, really?"
},
{
"start": 174.66,
"end": 174.86,
"text": "Yeah."
},
{
"start": 175.24,
"end": 176.28,
"text": "So Blanket's mother's black?"
},
{
"start": 176.32,
"end": 176.56,
"text": "Yeah."
},
{
"start": 177.54,
"end": 178.8,
"text": "But Blanket's so light."
},
{
"start": 179.7,
"end": 183.24,
"text": "Black people were called coloured people because we come in all colours."
},
{
"start": 184.08,
"end": 188.97,
"text": "From very white, as white as my hand, to very dark, it's the dark of your shirt."
},
{
"start": 189.44,
"end": 191.01,
"text": "My father has blue eyes."
},
{
"start": 192.93,
"end": 198.31,
"text": " And when they see Paris, they always think, Debbie, that could easily be my father's genes."
},
{
"start": 198.89,
"end": 199.17,
"text": "Really?"
},
{
"start": 199.67,
"end": 200.27,
"text": "Of course."
},
{
"start": 201.11,
"end": 202.97,
"text": "So when do you think you're going to have your next child?"
},
{
"start": 204.16,
"end": 205.34,
"text": "I wish I could have it today."
},
{
"start": 205.8,
"end": 206.06,
"text": "Really?"
},
{
"start": 207.04,
"end": 212.58,
"text": "I was thinking about adopting... ..two kids from each continent around the world."
},
{
"start": 214.1,
"end": 214.52,
"text": "Really?"
},
{
"start": 214.68,
"end": 214.92,
"text": "Yeah."
},
{
"start": 217.18,
"end": 217.78,
"text": "Boy and girl."
},
{
"start": 218.8,
"end": 219.86,
"text": "From every continent?"
},
{
"start": 219.94,
"end": 220.8,
"text": "On every continent."
},
{
"start": 221.19,
"end": 221.91,
"text": "That's my dream."
},
{
"start": 224.37,
"end": 230.41,
"text": " And so it was that we came back to our meeting at Neverland with 12-year-old Gavin."
},
{
"start": 231.27,
"end": 235.27,
"text": "I'd found this easily the most disturbing moment of the past eight months."
},
{
"start": 235.73,
"end": 240.91,
"text": "You know, some have, and they say, is that really appropriate?"
},
{
"start": 241.57,
"end": 248.66,
"text": "When you're talking about children, we met Gavin, and it was a great privilege to meet Gavin because he's had a lot of suffering in his life."
},
{
"start": 249.58,
"end": 252.18,
"text": "When Gavin was there, he talked about the fact that he shares your bedroom."
},
{
"start": 252.58,
"end": 253.1,
"text": "Yes."
},
{
"start": 254.24,
"end": 256.46,
"text": " Can you understand why people would worry about that?"
},
{
"start": 257.48,
"end": 258.38,
"text": "Because they're ignorant."
},
{
"start": 259.56,
"end": 268.15,
"text": "But is it really appropriate for a 44-year-old man to share a bedroom with a child who is not related to him at all?"
},
{
"start": 268.23,
"end": 269.31,
"text": "That's a beautiful thing."
},
{
"start": 269.81,
"end": 271.33,
"text": "That's not a worrying thing?"
},
{
"start": 271.75,
"end": 272.71,
"text": "Why should it be worrying?"
},
{
"start": 272.91,
"end": 273.95,
"text": "Who's the criminal?"
},
{
"start": 273.99,
"end": 275.27,
"text": "Who's Jack the Ripper in the room?"
},
{
"start": 277.04,
"end": 279.24,
"text": " This is a guy trying to help heal a child."
},
{
"start": 280.04,
"end": 281.98,
"text": "I'm sleeping in a sleeping bag on the floor."
},
{
"start": 282.38,
"end": 285.37,
"text": "I gave him the bed, because he has a brother named Star."
},
{
"start": 285.89,
"end": 289.19,
"text": "So him and Star took the bed, and I'm on the floor in the sleeping bag."
},
{
"start": 289.21,
"end": 290.61,
"text": "Did you ever sleep in the bed with them?"
},
{
"start": 290.81,
"end": 291.05,
"text": "No."
},
{
"start": 291.93,
"end": 293.51,
"text": "But I have slept in the bed with many children."
},
{
"start": 293.83,
"end": 295.01,
"text": "I sleep in the bed with all of them."
},
{
"start": 295.31,
"end": 299.3,
"text": "When Macaulay Culkin was little, Kieran Culkin would sleep on this side."
}
]
